From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:08:07 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 37/56] Plutonium: an archived or deleted thread's permission
 grants are forgotten

Plutonium's browser keeps a thread's permission decisions until a shell
revokes them. Whenever a thread is archived or deleted, by the user or an
agent, the server now asks the helper to forget them
(POST /v1/threads/<tag>/permissions/forget); the helper has a shell page do
it (shell.forgetThreadPermissions), or the next page to connect. A settled
thread keeps them. An older helper answers 404 and the grants stay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
